From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rumisle <why-excuse-quail@duck.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 02:45:24 +0800
Subject: app: drive the web app from the keyboard
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Web defaults where the browser keeps the desktop ones (custom keybinds
still win; the desktop app is unchanged): alt+T new session, alt+W close
tab, alt+shift+T reopen, alt+[ / alt+] previous / next tab, alt+I focus
input. With alt, digits and punctuation match the physical key, so the
Option key works on a Mac.

New everywhere: alt+1..9 go to a tab; alt+↑ / alt+↓ step through
messages and replies (each user message and the start of each reply;
past the last one follows the bottom again); PageUp / PageDown scroll
the transcript even while typing (other scrollers keep their keys);
alt+G stops the session from anywhere; alt+E edits the last message;
alt+C copies the last reply; alt+Y / alt+A / alt+N answer a permission
request; alt+/ opens Settings > Shortcuts. In the composer a single
Escape no longer stops a run: it asks for a second one within 1.5 s.

Ocelot-Patch: web/keyboard

